        "text": "**Defining the Approach**\n\nI'm solidifying the foundation, focusing on refreshing expired sessions within `refresh_session.py`. I'm leaning toward OAuth 2.0 with a refresh token as the core mechanism. Now, the main task is to select an external provider to make it specific and implementable.\n\n\n**Implementing Auth0 Refresh**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the specifics for the `refresh_session.py` file. I'm focusing on crafting the `refresh_access_token` function, which will handle the Auth0 interaction. The function needs to construct the Auth0 token endpoint URL and the payload for the POST request, including the grant type, client ID, secret, refresh token, and audience. I'll mock the `requests` library to simulate the HTTP call, and return the response.\n\n\n**Specifying the Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Auth0, and I'm integrating its specifics into `refresh_session.py`. The focus is now on the `refresh_access_token` function, which will handle the Auth0 interaction. I'm focusing on defining the endpoint URL and crafting the payload, including grant type, client ID, secret, refresh token, and audience. I'll continue to mock the `requests` library to simulate the HTTP call, and return the response. I'll assume some environment variables or placeholder values for domain, client ID, and client secret, for the time being.\n\n\n",
